To: gnats-bugs@NetBSD.org
Subject: inputmethod/anthy-elisp: accept emacs26 through emacs30, and fix last-command-char
From: zakinko@snowrabbit.org
Reply-To: zakinko@snowrabbit.org
X-send-pr-version: 3.95

>Submitter-Id:	net
>Originator:	Showta Ishizaki
>Organization:
>Confidential:	no
>Synopsis:	inputmethod/anthy-elisp: accept emacs26 through emacs30, and fix last-command-char
>Severity:	non-critical
>Priority:	low
>Category:	pkg
>Class:		change-request
>Release:	NetBSD 11.0, pkgsrc CVS as of 2026-08-14
>Environment:
System: NetBSD 11.0 i386
Architecture: i386
Machine: i386
>Description:
	inputmethod/anthy-elisp only accepts emacs21, emacs20 and XEmacs:

	  EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED= emacs21 emacs21nox emacs20 \
	                           xemacs215 xemacs215nox xemacs214 xemacs214nox

	so on a machine with a current Emacs it stops in can-be-built-here.mk.

	That line is not old.  It was added in rev 1.14 (2024-05-08, wiz):

	    anthy-elisp: restrict emacs versions

	    Since I don't know better, restrict it to the versions that were
	    available at the time of the packaged version of this software
	    (2009).

	Before 1.14 the package had no EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED at all and took
	whatever was installed.  So the restriction was a guess made in the
	absence of a test, and this PR is the test.

	It matters because anthy-elisp is the only package that installs
	anthy.el -- the other three in the tree that ship one are all tamago.
	An init file that does

	  (load-library "anthy")
	  (setq default-input-method 'japanese-anthy)

	has no other way to work through pkgsrc.

	Widening the list is not enough on its own, though.  anthy.el uses two
	names that Emacs has since removed.

	The one that stops the build is at top level, anthy.el line 74:

	  (set-face-underline-p 'anthy-highlight-face t)

	set-face-underline-p became an alias for set-face-underline in Emacs
	24.3 and was removed in Emacs 29 (NEWS.29 lists it among the obsolete
	items removed).  Because the call is at top level, loading anthy.el on
	Emacs 29 or 30 signals an error, so anthy-isearch.el and anthy-kyuri.el
	fail to byte-compile -- both do nothing but (require 'anthy) at the
	line the compiler names -- and the build ends with

	  ERROR: The following files are in the PLIST but not in .../usr/pkg:
	  ERROR:         .../share/emacs/site-lisp/anthy/anthy-isearch.elc
	  ERROR:         .../share/emacs/site-lisp/anthy/anthy-kyuri.elc

	Emacs 20, 21 and 23 have only the -p name, so the call is guarded with
	fboundp rather than renamed.

	The other one does not stop the build.  anthy.el's own compatibility
	shim returns last-command-char on the GNU Emacs branch:

	  (defun anthy-last-command-char ()
	    (if anthy-xemacs
	        (let ((event last-command-event))
	          ...)
	      last-command-char))

	last-command-char was removed in Emacs 24 -- NEWS.24, under "Some
	obsolete functions, variables, and faces have been removed", lists
	'last-input-char', 'last-command-char' and 'unread-command-char'.  The
	XEmacs branch already uses the right name; only the GNU Emacs branch
	was left behind.  That reference is inside a function, so byte
	compilation merely warns, and the package installs -- and then
	japanese-anthy fails the moment a key is typed.

>How-To-Repeat:
	cd /usr/pkgsrc/inputmethod/anthy-elisp
	make EMACS_TYPE=emacs26nox fetch

	  ERROR: [can-be-built-here.mk] This package has PKG_FAIL_REASON set:
	  ERROR: Accepted versions are: emacs21 emacs21nox emacs20 xemacs215 xemacs215nox xemacs214 xemacs214nox
	  ERROR: No valid Emacs version installed found

	EMACS_TYPE has to go on the command line rather than in the
	environment; if mk.conf sets it, the environment does not win.

>Fix:
	Two parts.

	EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED gains emacs26 through emacs30.  Together with
	the emacs20, emacs21 and XEmacs entries already there, that is every
	Emacs pkgsrc offers -- there is no emacs22 through emacs25 package.

	patch-src-util_anthy.el guards the set-face-underline-p call with
	fboundp and changes last-command-char to last-command-event.  anthy has
	not been released since 2009, so there is nowhere upstream to send
	those.

	The patch goes in inputmethod/anthy/patches because anthy-elisp shares
	PATCHDIR and DISTINFO_FILE with inputmethod/anthy.  It sorts after the
	existing patch-anthy.el and the two touch different parts of the file.
	inputmethod/anthy installs no .el files of its own, so its PKGREVISION
	is left alone; anthy-elisp's is bumped.

	XXX-CI: build result to be filled in before sending.

	Index: inputmethod/anthy-elisp/Makefile
	===================================================================
	RCS file: /cvsroot/pkgsrc/inputmethod/anthy-elisp/Makefile,v
	retrieving revision 1.14
	diff -u -r1.14 Makefile
	--- inputmethod/anthy-elisp/Makefile	8 May 2024 12:20:52 -0000	1.14
	+++ inputmethod/anthy-elisp/Makefile	14 Aug 2026 19:27:02 -0000
	@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
	 
	 .include	"../../inputmethod/anthy/Makefile.common"
	 PKGNAME=	${EMACS_PKGNAME_PREFIX}anthy-elisp-${ANTHY_VERSION}
	-PKGREVISION=	6
	+PKGREVISION=	7
	 CATEGORIES=	inputmethod editors
	 
	 MAINTAINER=	taya@NetBSD.org
	@@ -14,7 +14,13 @@
	 CONFIGURE_ENV+=	EMACS=${EMACS_BIN:Q}
	 EMACS_MODULES+=	base leim
	 
	-EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED=	emacs21 emacs21nox emacs20 xemacs215 xemacs215nox xemacs214 xemacs214nox
	+EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED=	emacs21 emacs21nox emacs20
	+EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED+=	xemacs215 xemacs215nox xemacs214 xemacs214nox
	+EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED+=	emacs26 emacs26nox
	+EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED+=	emacs27 emacs27nox
	+EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED+=	emacs28 emacs28nox
	+EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED+=	emacs29 emacs29nox
	+EMACS_VERSIONS_ACCEPTED+=	emacs30 emacs30nox
	 
	 .include "../../editors/emacs/modules.mk"
	 
